# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRODUCTION environment — loaded automatically by `npm run build`.
#
# Vite reads this file whenever it builds in `production` mode, which `npm run
# build` does by default. There is no `--mode` flag in the build script and none
# is wanted: this dashboard has one deployment shape.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS COMMITTED, AND EVERYTHING IN IT IS PUBLIC BY CONSTRUCTION.
#   Vite inlines every `VITE_`-prefixed value into the JavaScript bundle, which
#   is downloaded by every browser that loads the dashboard. A value here is
#   readable by anyone who opens the page — so nothing secret may ever be added.
#   There is nothing secret to add: the dashboard authenticates with cookies the
#   service sets, and holds no API key of its own.
#
# ⚠ THE VALUES ARE BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME, NOT READ AT RUN TIME. Changing this
#   file does nothing to a running container; it takes a new image. That is why
#   the image is built per branch and why `production` is the only branch that
#   produces a deployable one.
#
# `.env.local` still overrides this file and is still git-ignored, so a
# developer pointing at their own machine is unaffected by anything here.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED — the wi-admin service, including the version segment.
#
# ⚠ `admin-api`, not `api`. Those are two different services: `api.wi-mall.com`
#   is jovi-mall (commerce) and this dashboard never calls it. wi-admin serves
#   everything under /api/v1 and is the only backend this app talks to — there
#   is no second base URL and no second token.
#
# Verified reachable and CORS-allowlisted for https://admin.wi-mall.com on
# 2026-09-13: a preflight from that origin returns 204 with a matching
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin and Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://admin-api.wi-mall.com/api/v1

# App display name — browser title and sidebar wordmark.
VITE_APP_NAME=WiMall Admin

# ─── Deliberately unset ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# VITE_NOTIFICATIONS_POLL_MS — the unread-count poll interval. The code default
# is the considered one; overriding it here would be tuning without a
# measurement. There is no realtime transport on this service (no WebSocket, no
# SSE), so this poll is the whole notification mechanism — lower it only with a
# reason, because it multiplies across every open dashboard tab.
